00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:31,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:32,470 --> 00:00:39,477
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:01:13,011 --> 00:01:13,928
‎Grandfather.

3
00:01:17,515 --> 00:01:18,349
‎Why?

4
00:01:19,976 --> 00:01:21,728
‎Why do you hate me so much?

5
00:01:22,353 --> 00:01:24,314
‎Because you have no talent.

6
00:01:24,397 --> 00:01:26,316
‎It's time to give up.

7
00:01:27,192 --> 00:01:29,485
‎You'll never make it.

8
00:01:30,069 --> 00:01:30,904
‎Grandfather…

9
00:01:33,948 --> 00:01:37,327
‎But I love music too.

10
00:01:40,830 --> 00:01:43,958
‎I love it so much.

11
00:01:45,209 --> 00:01:46,127
‎So why do you say…

12
00:01:48,504 --> 00:01:49,839
‎I'll never make it?

13
00:01:58,473 --> 00:01:59,599
‎Why not me?

14
00:02:01,935 --> 00:02:03,186
‎Why?

15
00:02:06,689 --> 00:02:10,652
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

16
00:02:16,157 --> 00:02:17,200
‎Why not me…

17
00:02:17,283 --> 00:02:18,993
‎EPISODE 5

18
00:02:20,078 --> 00:02:20,995
‎Why?

19
00:02:21,913 --> 00:02:22,997
‎-Why?
‎-Pi-o.

20
00:02:25,917 --> 00:02:27,126
‎Pi-o, what's wrong?

21
00:02:28,544 --> 00:02:29,837
‎Did you have another nightmare?

22
00:02:30,380 --> 00:02:31,339
‎No.

23
00:02:33,007 --> 00:02:34,008
‎Tell me.

24
00:02:35,176 --> 00:02:37,971
‎What nightmare wakes you up
‎every 30 minutes?

25
00:02:40,932 --> 00:02:42,100
‎Don't worry about it.

26
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:59,867
‎CHOI JEONG-YO

27
00:03:17,510 --> 00:03:19,262
‎Why do you keep calling?

28
00:03:19,345 --> 00:03:20,555
‎I'm sorry.

29
00:03:20,638 --> 00:03:21,889
‎I'm really sorry,

30
00:03:23,141 --> 00:03:26,853
‎but I'm outside the hospital
‎and would like to check in on Pi-o.

31
00:03:27,562 --> 00:03:29,188
‎How many times do I have to tell you?

32
00:03:29,981 --> 00:03:31,858
‎Pi-o doesn't want to see you.

33
00:03:32,608 --> 00:03:33,526
‎Don't you get it?

34
00:03:33,609 --> 00:03:34,610
‎But I…

35
00:03:48,207 --> 00:03:49,542
‎Why are you up?

36
00:03:51,419 --> 00:03:52,295
‎Get some more sleep.

37
00:03:58,384 --> 00:03:59,427
‎Was it Jeong-yo?

38
00:04:02,430 --> 00:04:03,264
‎No.

39
00:04:03,348 --> 00:04:04,891
‎Please call Jeong-yo for me.

40
00:04:06,642 --> 00:04:07,602
‎I need to talk to him.

41
00:04:08,478 --> 00:04:10,063
‎About what?

42
00:04:10,146 --> 00:04:11,606
‎Just wait until you're discharged.

43
00:04:11,689 --> 00:04:12,815
‎I said call him.

44
00:04:14,484 --> 00:04:15,318
‎Call Jeong-yo.

45
00:04:23,826 --> 00:04:24,827
‎KANG PI-O (MALE, 16 YEARS OLD)

46
00:04:29,749 --> 00:04:30,583
‎Thank you.

47
00:04:40,259 --> 00:04:41,594
‎Are you feeling better now?

48
00:04:42,553 --> 00:04:43,388
‎Yeah.

49
00:04:44,472 --> 00:04:45,348
‎Hey.

50
00:04:46,015 --> 00:04:49,060
‎Hospitalized for pneumonia?
‎What are you, a little kid?

51
00:04:49,143 --> 00:04:52,814
‎This is why I've been telling you
‎to eat and sleep well.

52
00:04:58,986 --> 00:05:00,113
‎When are you getting discharged?

53
00:05:01,072 --> 00:05:02,198
‎-Soon.
‎-Soon?

54
00:05:05,368 --> 00:05:07,245
‎Don't stay too long, okay?

55
00:05:07,328 --> 00:05:10,498
‎I'm bored out of my mind
‎because you're not around.

56
00:05:11,332 --> 00:05:13,876
‎Han-rim and Seok-hwan
‎are so full of themselves these days.

57
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:15,670
‎They've been acting up,

58
00:05:15,753 --> 00:05:17,463
‎and it's driving me crazy.

59
00:05:18,631 --> 00:05:19,757
‎Jeez.

60
00:05:25,054 --> 00:05:26,722
‎I wanted to tell you something.

61
00:05:26,806 --> 00:05:27,932
‎You did?

62
00:05:29,517 --> 00:05:32,520
‎Go ahead. Tell me whatever it is.

63
00:05:37,525 --> 00:05:39,026
‎After I get discharged…

64
00:05:41,279 --> 00:05:43,030
‎I'm going to prepare
‎for the Harmonie Competition.

65
00:05:43,865 --> 00:05:44,949
‎The competition?

66
00:05:45,032 --> 00:05:47,451
‎I thought you didn't want to
‎enter competitions anymore.

67
00:05:48,828 --> 00:05:50,913
‎How else can I prove myself if I don't?

68
00:05:51,497 --> 00:05:52,874
‎But still,

69
00:05:53,833 --> 00:05:55,877
‎I thought you wanted to
‎be happy making music.

70
00:05:56,419 --> 00:05:59,297
‎You said you were
‎tired of competing, so why?

71
00:05:59,380 --> 00:06:00,298
‎I'm not a genius.

72
00:06:01,757 --> 00:06:04,677
‎If I don't prove myself on stage,
‎who will listen to me play?

73
00:06:06,929 --> 00:06:08,472
‎The reason I called you here

74
00:06:09,807 --> 00:06:11,100
‎is to ask you…

75
00:06:12,852 --> 00:06:14,312
‎to enter the same competition.

76
00:06:14,854 --> 00:06:15,688
‎What?

77
00:06:16,272 --> 00:06:17,481
‎Don't say no.

78
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:20,651
‎If I'm really your friend,

79
00:06:21,986 --> 00:06:23,738
‎you'll do me this favor.

80
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:26,908
‎-But that's just--
‎-Why?

81
00:06:27,992 --> 00:06:30,077
‎Do you think you're guaranteed to win?

82
00:06:30,995 --> 00:06:34,040
‎You're wrong.
‎Things won't go your way this time.

83
00:06:34,832 --> 00:06:35,750
‎I already told you.

84
00:06:36,959 --> 00:06:39,545
‎I'll do whatever it takes to prove myself.

85
00:06:40,504 --> 00:06:42,173
‎But don't you dare lose on purpose.

86
00:06:43,424 --> 00:06:45,259
‎If I catch wind of that…

87
00:06:47,678 --> 00:06:49,180
‎I'm going to kill you.

88
00:06:54,018 --> 00:06:54,894
‎Fine.

89
00:06:58,439 --> 00:07:01,359
‎But you'd better practice really hard,

90
00:07:01,442 --> 00:07:03,527
‎or I'll wipe the floor with you.

91
00:07:05,488 --> 00:07:07,114
‎By the way, you can't kill me.

92
00:07:18,084 --> 00:07:19,168
‎You made the right call.

93
00:07:20,586 --> 00:07:22,296
‎Like you said, placing in competitions

94
00:07:23,422 --> 00:07:25,508
‎is the only way to play professionally.

95
00:07:25,591 --> 00:07:27,760
‎-Let's prepare well and--
‎-Don't get excited.

96
00:07:28,844 --> 00:07:30,304
‎If I don't win the competition…

97
00:07:33,849 --> 00:07:35,226
‎I'm going to quit the piano.

98
00:07:36,185 --> 00:07:37,645
‎I'd rather quit…

99
00:07:40,523 --> 00:07:41,566
‎than be a mediocre pianist.

100
00:07:47,071 --> 00:07:48,197
‎Do you want to

101
00:07:48,864 --> 00:07:50,283
‎enter the competition?

102
00:07:52,910 --> 00:07:53,744
‎No.

103
00:07:54,328 --> 00:07:55,413
‎Then why are you doing it?

104
00:07:56,539 --> 00:07:57,790
‎I have to enter…

105
00:08:00,876 --> 00:08:03,546
‎to help Pi-o get back on his feet.

106
00:08:07,758 --> 00:08:10,011
‎If he needs me to light a fire under him,

107
00:08:11,637 --> 00:08:13,514
‎I'll gladly do it.

108
00:08:16,767 --> 00:08:17,643
‎All right.

109
00:08:18,978 --> 00:08:20,396
‎Let's do it.

110
00:08:20,479 --> 00:08:21,314
‎Okay.

111
00:08:21,397 --> 00:08:23,691
‎But I need you to promise me something.

112
00:08:24,317 --> 00:08:26,235
‎If you're just going to
‎play a supporting role,

113
00:08:27,570 --> 00:08:28,571
‎stop right now.

114
00:08:30,156 --> 00:08:31,949
‎I care for you and Pi-o

115
00:08:32,658 --> 00:08:34,660
‎equally as my students.

116
00:08:37,830 --> 00:08:40,041
‎If I catch you not giving it your all,

117
00:08:41,626 --> 00:08:43,628
‎I won't let it slide.

118
00:08:49,008 --> 00:08:50,593
‎Why is he wearing headphones during lunch?

119
00:08:50,676 --> 00:08:51,844
‎Seriously.

120
00:09:48,442 --> 00:09:49,860
‎Congratulations.

121
00:10:29,525 --> 00:10:31,110
‎Good afternoon, contestants.

122
00:10:31,193 --> 00:10:34,196
‎Congratulations on advancing
‎to the main round

123
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:37,366
‎of the Prague Harmonie
‎International Competition.

124
00:10:40,286 --> 00:10:43,748
‎First, allow me to outline
‎the competition schedule.

125
00:10:44,665 --> 00:10:47,543
‎This week, 24 contestants

126
00:10:47,626 --> 00:10:51,630
‎will be selected from
‎approximately 60 main round participants

127
00:10:52,131 --> 00:10:54,258
‎to advance to the semifinals.

128
00:10:54,341 --> 00:10:58,637
‎Those 24 semifinalists
‎will be competing next week.

129
00:10:59,472 --> 00:11:02,475
‎From there, 12 finalists will be chosen,

130
00:11:02,558 --> 00:11:05,644
‎and they will move
‎from their homestays to the chapel

131
00:11:06,562 --> 00:11:09,273
‎where all mobile phones
‎and electronic devices

132
00:11:09,356 --> 00:11:10,858
‎will be confiscated.

133
00:11:11,734 --> 00:11:14,403
‎And they will reside together
‎for one week.

134
00:11:14,487 --> 00:11:17,948
‎SEMIFINALS
‎QUALIFYING ROUND FOR THE TOP 24

135
00:11:18,657 --> 00:11:20,910
‎Contestant number 15,

136
00:11:20,993 --> 00:11:24,121
‎Jeong-yo Choi, please come to the stage.

137
00:12:15,839 --> 00:12:17,174
‎You've got to be kidding me.

138
00:12:18,133 --> 00:12:19,176
‎Where'd this guy come from?

139
00:12:19,260 --> 00:12:22,346
‎I have no idea, but damn it,
‎he's ridiculously good.

140
00:12:52,001 --> 00:12:52,960
‎Fine.

141
00:12:53,544 --> 00:12:54,753
‎His technique, yeah.

142
00:12:55,671 --> 00:12:58,299
‎Genuinely… untouchable.

143
00:12:59,592 --> 00:13:01,093
‎No one even comes close to that.

144
00:13:24,116 --> 00:13:25,743
‎What's wrong with your pinky finger?

145
00:13:30,623 --> 00:13:32,666
‎If you keep playing, you'll destroy it.

146
00:13:33,626 --> 00:13:35,711
‎Give practice a rest
‎and get it treated first.

147
00:13:37,296 --> 00:13:39,423
‎I don't know what you saw,
‎but stop being dramatic.

148
00:13:39,506 --> 00:13:41,425
‎Mind your own business
‎and worry about yourself.

149
00:14:01,528 --> 00:14:02,571
‎You're okay, right?

150
00:14:03,656 --> 00:14:04,865
‎Are you taking

151
00:14:05,741 --> 00:14:07,034
‎your medication?

152
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:08,994
‎Yes.

153
00:14:09,578 --> 00:14:10,537
‎Good.

154
00:14:11,455 --> 00:14:13,666
‎Hang in there for three more weeks.

155
00:14:14,625 --> 00:14:17,753
‎I'll get stronger meds from the hospital,
‎so just bear with it.

156
00:14:17,836 --> 00:14:19,254
‎We've worked too hard to get here.

157
00:14:20,255 --> 00:14:21,382
‎It'd be such a shame

158
00:14:22,633 --> 00:14:25,302
‎to give up now after all this, right?

159
00:15:25,946 --> 00:15:26,989
‎Where have you been?

160
00:15:29,575 --> 00:15:31,118
‎Why aren't you in bed?

161
00:15:32,619 --> 00:15:33,912
‎Have you been practicing until now?

162
00:15:34,705 --> 00:15:36,790
‎What if you wear yourself out?

163
00:15:37,374 --> 00:15:40,002
‎Is it unusual to practice until 4 a.m.?

164
00:15:40,586 --> 00:15:44,339
‎Or is it unusual to be out
‎until this hour?

165
00:15:46,175 --> 00:15:49,386
‎I went for a drive because I'm jet-lagged.

166
00:15:49,470 --> 00:15:50,763
‎Go to bed.

167
00:15:50,846 --> 00:15:54,099
‎It'll only get tougher starting tomorrow,
‎so you need to pace yourself.

168
00:16:00,898 --> 00:16:04,985
‎TOP 12 FINALIST ANNOUNCEMENT

169
00:16:05,486 --> 00:16:07,279
‎The first finalist is

170
00:16:07,905 --> 00:16:09,031
‎Pi-o Kang.

171
00:16:23,045 --> 00:16:24,963
‎The second finalist is

172
00:16:25,798 --> 00:16:26,965
‎Jeong-yo Choi.

173
00:16:37,601 --> 00:16:39,228
‎The third finalist is

174
00:16:39,978 --> 00:16:41,188
‎Tom Harrison.

175
00:17:07,798 --> 00:17:09,216
‎Welcome to the chapel.

176
00:17:09,299 --> 00:17:13,137
‎From this point on,
‎no outsiders are permitted.

177
00:17:13,220 --> 00:17:16,140
‎You may say your goodbyes
‎to your mother here.

178
00:17:17,474 --> 00:17:19,685
‎You'll do great, right?

179
00:17:21,395 --> 00:17:22,229
‎Yes.

180
00:17:31,488 --> 00:17:32,865
‎As you already know,

181
00:17:32,948 --> 00:17:36,201
‎I'm sure you chose a free piece
‎you're confident in,

182
00:17:36,285 --> 00:17:39,872
‎but the assigned piece is
‎far more difficult than you can imagine.

183
00:17:40,747 --> 00:17:45,502
‎Since it's a contemporary piece,
‎interpreting it won't be easy either.

184
00:17:46,086 --> 00:17:46,962
‎So…

185
00:17:48,964 --> 00:17:51,633
‎You must not lose
‎the set piece sheet music

186
00:17:51,717 --> 00:17:53,802
‎under any circumstances.

187
00:17:53,886 --> 00:17:56,680
‎If it's lost due to your own negligence,

188
00:17:56,763 --> 00:17:58,265
‎it will not be reissued.

189
00:18:04,521 --> 00:18:06,523
‎Now, your phone please.

190
00:18:09,902 --> 00:18:10,777
‎Here it is.

191
00:18:11,612 --> 00:18:12,654
‎Good luck.

192
00:18:12,738 --> 00:18:13,947
‎Thank you.

193
00:19:07,668 --> 00:19:09,002
‎As of today,

194
00:19:09,086 --> 00:19:12,381
‎all 12 finalists
‎officially moved into the chapel.

195
00:19:13,507 --> 00:19:17,177
‎Tomorrow, reporters from around the world
‎will be arriving.

196
00:19:17,678 --> 00:19:21,056
‎After that, performances
‎will take place in order,

197
00:19:21,556 --> 00:19:23,267
‎two contestants at a time.

198
00:19:24,268 --> 00:19:29,982
‎This will be the first
‎and last banquet with everyone,

199
00:19:30,065 --> 00:19:33,026
‎so please enjoy the meal.

200
00:19:44,288 --> 00:19:45,622
‎How's your pinky finger?

201
00:19:47,332 --> 00:19:48,917
‎I said mind your own business.

202
00:19:49,001 --> 00:19:51,295
‎This is the last time
‎I'm asking, you punk.

203
00:19:53,297 --> 00:19:56,174
‎We don't even have time to eat right now,
‎and they're talking about a banquet?

204
00:19:57,009 --> 00:19:59,386
‎Honestly, I'd much rather just have
‎one more day to practice.

205
00:19:59,469 --> 00:20:03,432
‎Like, how exactly are we supposed to
‎master two pieces in seven days?

206
00:20:03,515 --> 00:20:04,725
‎That's crazy, right?

207
00:20:04,808 --> 00:20:06,393
‎I mean, that's exactly what I'm saying.

208
00:20:07,102 --> 00:20:10,063
‎Like, the pressure is so intense,
‎I can't even sleep.

209
00:20:11,106 --> 00:20:12,983
‎How is everyone doing with the set piece?

210
00:20:13,066 --> 00:20:16,028
‎Isn't this the hardest song
‎we have ever gotten?

211
00:20:16,111 --> 00:20:18,780
‎I have been analyzing the score for days,

212
00:20:18,864 --> 00:20:20,198
‎and I still have no clue.

213
00:20:21,992 --> 00:20:24,077
‎Hey, how about you guys?

214
00:20:24,745 --> 00:20:25,996
‎How's the set piece for you?

215
00:20:26,079 --> 00:20:27,080
‎Pretty easy?

216
00:20:27,831 --> 00:20:29,124
‎Must have been easy.

217
00:20:29,207 --> 00:20:32,085
‎There's apparently no such thing
‎as a difficult piece for the Koreans.

218
00:20:33,211 --> 00:20:34,671
‎Absolute practice addicts.

219
00:20:36,590 --> 00:20:39,217
‎Hey, what did she just say?

220
00:20:39,301 --> 00:20:40,427
‎Was she talking trash?

221
00:20:40,510 --> 00:20:42,512
‎She's asking if we find the set piece
‎easy or hard.

222
00:20:45,807 --> 00:20:47,017
‎Difficult, difficult.

223
00:20:48,143 --> 00:20:49,311
‎Hard, hard.

224
00:20:49,895 --> 00:20:52,689
‎But hard training, good.

225
00:20:53,190 --> 00:20:54,691
‎Then what did you pick
‎for your free piece?

226
00:20:54,775 --> 00:20:55,942
‎"Beep beep?"

227
00:20:56,026 --> 00:20:57,527
‎Free piece.

228
00:21:01,531 --> 00:21:02,866
‎She's asking what piece you prepared.

229
00:21:06,119 --> 00:21:08,997
‎Rachmaninoff's Concerto No. 2.

230
00:21:19,007 --> 00:21:20,008
‎The second concerto?

231
00:21:22,052 --> 00:21:23,929
‎I want to play the third one.

232
00:21:24,554 --> 00:21:25,722
‎No.

233
00:21:25,806 --> 00:21:27,099
‎In my opinion,

234
00:21:27,724 --> 00:21:31,061
‎the piece that will help you
‎grow more in the long run

235
00:21:31,144 --> 00:21:32,771
‎is the second one.

236
00:21:33,355 --> 00:21:34,731
‎But I find the third one

237
00:21:35,899 --> 00:21:38,360
‎-easier than the second.
‎-Pi-o.

238
00:21:38,443 --> 00:21:40,779
‎Technique shouldn't be your main goal.

239
00:21:40,862 --> 00:21:43,824
‎You need to choose a piece
‎based on musicality and emotion.

240
00:21:44,449 --> 00:21:46,326
‎You need to push past your limits

241
00:21:47,244 --> 00:21:48,745
‎to win in the end.

242
00:21:50,789 --> 00:21:51,665
‎Pi-o.

243
00:21:53,291 --> 00:21:54,251
‎Have faith in yourself.

244
00:21:56,753 --> 00:21:58,839
‎Why did he have us play the same piece?

245
00:22:49,556 --> 00:22:51,224
‎Do you have any idea what time it is?

246
00:22:51,308 --> 00:22:52,309
‎Why should I?

247
00:22:52,392 --> 00:22:53,643
‎How am I supposed to sleep

248
00:22:53,727 --> 00:22:56,521
‎when all I can hear
‎is the sound of that damn piano?

249
00:22:56,605 --> 00:22:58,023
‎Take it to the administration.

250
00:22:58,106 --> 00:23:01,193
‎It's not my fault
‎the rooms aren't soundproof!

251
00:23:01,693 --> 00:23:02,694
‎Hey, hey!

252
00:23:03,737 --> 00:23:05,488
‎Open the damn door!

253
00:23:05,572 --> 00:23:06,489
‎Pi-o!

254
00:23:07,699 --> 00:23:10,744
‎You bastard, open the door!
‎I said right now!

255
00:23:11,578 --> 00:23:12,996
‎Open the door!

256
00:23:13,747 --> 00:23:17,042
‎No easy. Little bit difficult.

257
00:23:17,125 --> 00:23:19,002
‎-Just a little bit? Okay.
‎-Yes, a little bit.

258
00:23:19,586 --> 00:23:20,420
‎And…

259
00:23:20,503 --> 00:23:21,796
‎So despite your young age,

260
00:23:21,880 --> 00:23:24,216
‎you've amazed the world
‎with flawless technique.

261
00:23:24,299 --> 00:23:25,759
‎How did you start to play the piano?

262
00:23:27,928 --> 00:23:30,222
‎I was told that my family noticed me

263
00:23:30,305 --> 00:23:34,267
‎play songs from TV
‎when I was around three years old.

264
00:23:34,351 --> 00:23:35,477
‎Three years old?

265
00:23:36,311 --> 00:23:37,604
‎So you are a genius.

266
00:23:38,605 --> 00:23:42,067
‎I heard that you're the grandson
‎of Maestro Seung-woon Kang.

267
00:23:42,150 --> 00:23:46,154
‎His fans are eagerly wondering
‎whether we might see a collaboration

268
00:23:46,238 --> 00:23:48,990
‎-between a grandfather as a conductor
‎-Music made me powerful…

269
00:23:49,074 --> 00:23:51,243
‎and his grandson as a pianist.

270
00:23:51,326 --> 00:23:52,369
‎Did you hear that?

271
00:23:54,621 --> 00:23:55,622
‎I'd like that.

272
00:24:20,939 --> 00:24:21,815
‎Go ahead.

273
00:24:24,109 --> 00:24:25,652
‎Start from the coda
‎of the second movement.

274
00:24:25,735 --> 00:24:29,906
‎CODA: ITALIAN FOR "TAIL,"
‎THE MEMORABLE CLOSING SECTION OF A PIECE

275
00:25:23,501 --> 00:25:24,586
‎Stop.

276
00:25:31,468 --> 00:25:32,552
‎You'd be better off…

277
00:25:35,013 --> 00:25:37,640
‎asking Baryshnikov to do it instead of me.

278
00:25:40,477 --> 00:25:41,770
‎Why?

279
00:25:42,479 --> 00:25:45,273
‎Because he'd be a better fit
‎for your performance.

280
00:25:48,860 --> 00:25:50,403
‎Please tell me why.

281
00:25:51,738 --> 00:25:53,198
‎You'd conduct for anyone else.

282
00:25:53,281 --> 00:25:55,658
‎No, I know you'll conduct for Jeong-yo.

283
00:25:56,534 --> 00:25:58,244
‎But why are you refusing me?

284
00:26:01,456 --> 00:26:02,916
‎I just told you.

285
00:26:04,125 --> 00:26:06,878
‎He'd be a better fit for your performance.

286
00:26:06,961 --> 00:26:09,881
‎We're both conductors for the competition,
‎so what's the problem?

287
00:26:37,867 --> 00:26:38,701
‎What are you doing?

288
00:26:40,328 --> 00:26:41,704
‎Why are you lurking like that?

289
00:27:03,351 --> 00:27:04,394
‎Pi-o.

290
00:27:04,477 --> 00:27:06,271
‎Technique shouldn't be your main goal.

291
00:27:06,354 --> 00:27:09,315
‎You need to choose a piece
‎based on musicality and emotion.

292
00:27:18,741 --> 00:27:20,326
‎You'd be better off…

293
00:27:20,410 --> 00:27:23,580
‎asking Baryshnikov to do it
‎instead of me.

294
00:27:23,663 --> 00:27:25,206
‎I just told you.

295
00:27:25,290 --> 00:27:27,417
‎He'd be a better fit for your performance.

296
00:27:28,251 --> 00:27:29,085
‎Pi-o Kang!

297
00:27:29,669 --> 00:27:31,379
‎Enough is enough!

298
00:27:31,463 --> 00:27:33,214
‎How many days has it been, huh?

299
00:27:33,298 --> 00:27:35,091
‎You trying to ruin my competition?

300
00:27:36,468 --> 00:27:37,677
‎If you can't stand it,

301
00:27:37,760 --> 00:27:39,345
‎ask them to switch your room.

302
00:27:39,429 --> 00:27:40,680
‎Why do you keep harassing me?

303
00:27:40,763 --> 00:27:42,724
‎No, no, I told you to switch

304
00:27:42,807 --> 00:27:45,059
‎because the piano in that room
‎suits me best.

305
00:27:45,143 --> 00:27:46,519
‎Don't be stupid.

306
00:27:46,603 --> 00:27:48,354
‎Why would I waste my time like that?

307
00:27:50,690 --> 00:27:52,400
‎You selfish bastard.

308
00:27:52,484 --> 00:27:54,694
‎Spying on people, huh? Like a rat!

309
00:27:56,613 --> 00:27:58,239
‎Hey, knock it off!

310
00:27:58,823 --> 00:28:00,783
‎Stop, stop!

311
00:28:00,867 --> 00:28:01,826
‎Cut it out.

312
00:28:01,910 --> 00:28:04,287
‎Do you want to get kicked out
‎before you even compete?

313
00:28:04,787 --> 00:28:07,415
‎He's just defending you because
‎you guys are from the same country.

314
00:28:07,499 --> 00:28:08,625
‎It's pathetic.

315
00:28:08,708 --> 00:28:11,377
‎Does he even know that you've been
‎eavesdropping on his performance?

316
00:28:11,461 --> 00:28:12,295
‎Shut up!

317
00:28:12,378 --> 00:28:14,255
‎Hey, I said knock it off!

318
00:28:14,339 --> 00:28:15,423
‎You crazy bastard.

319
00:28:15,507 --> 00:28:16,716
‎Out, now!

320
00:28:17,300 --> 00:28:18,510
‎What a psychopath!

321
00:28:19,093 --> 00:28:20,303
‎Come on!

322
00:28:25,600 --> 00:28:27,185
‎You need to eat as you practice

323
00:28:27,268 --> 00:28:30,021
‎so you can actually fight back
‎at times like this.

324
00:28:33,691 --> 00:28:35,193
‎You're not yourself right now.

325
00:28:35,276 --> 00:28:37,487
‎Stop stressing and get a hold of yourself.

326
00:28:38,029 --> 00:28:40,865
‎Go take a walk and get some good sleep.

327
00:28:41,574 --> 00:28:44,452
‎Practicing all night won't help.

328
00:28:44,536 --> 00:28:47,413
‎Guys like you can afford that luxury.

329
00:28:47,997 --> 00:28:51,042
‎You know practice is everything
‎to people like me.

330
00:28:51,835 --> 00:28:52,961
‎Get out of my way.

331
00:28:53,044 --> 00:28:55,046
‎Come on, Pi-o!

332
00:28:55,129 --> 00:28:57,131
‎I said get out of my way!

333
00:29:47,181 --> 00:29:48,182
‎Open the door.

334
00:29:49,434 --> 00:29:50,768
‎Open the door!

335
00:29:53,313 --> 00:29:54,647
‎What is it now? Hey!

336
00:29:55,648 --> 00:29:56,900
‎What are you doing?

337
00:29:57,483 --> 00:29:58,651
‎This is my room. Get out!

338
00:30:00,862 --> 00:30:02,363
‎What are you doing?

339
00:30:04,782 --> 00:30:05,783
‎What are you doing?

340
00:30:06,659 --> 00:30:08,286
‎Where'd you hide my sheet music?

341
00:30:08,369 --> 00:30:09,662
‎What the hell are you talking about?

342
00:30:10,580 --> 00:30:13,875
‎You stole it to screw me over
‎while I was gone.

343
00:30:13,958 --> 00:30:15,376
‎Why on earth are you in here?

344
00:30:15,460 --> 00:30:16,836
‎Use your words!

345
00:30:16,920 --> 00:30:18,296
‎You're insane.

346
00:30:18,379 --> 00:30:20,048
‎Where's my sheet music?

347
00:30:24,385 --> 00:30:26,512
‎Pi-o. Kang Pi-o!

348
00:30:26,596 --> 00:30:27,972
‎He's lost it.

349
00:30:28,056 --> 00:30:30,266
‎Pi-o, you're completely insane!

350
00:30:41,027 --> 00:30:41,945
‎Pi-o.

351
00:30:45,490 --> 00:30:46,449
‎Kang Pi-o!

352
00:30:54,207 --> 00:30:55,166
‎No.

353
00:30:59,629 --> 00:31:00,630
‎Kang Pi-o!

354
00:31:03,883 --> 00:31:05,259
‎Hey, stop!

355
00:31:05,343 --> 00:31:06,302
‎Let go of me!

356
00:31:07,095 --> 00:31:08,179
‎Come on, get out!

357
00:31:08,680 --> 00:31:09,847
‎I said let go!

358
00:31:14,143 --> 00:31:15,395
‎Come on.

359
00:31:15,478 --> 00:31:16,646
‎Get out!

360
00:31:18,022 --> 00:31:18,856
‎Enough!

361
00:31:27,281 --> 00:31:28,700
‎Are you insane?

362
00:31:28,783 --> 00:31:29,867
‎This is all your fault.

363
00:31:30,493 --> 00:31:32,120
‎It's all your fault!

364
00:31:42,296 --> 00:31:43,673
‎It's just the piano.

365
00:31:44,632 --> 00:31:46,384
‎Why tear yourself apart over music?

366
00:31:47,552 --> 00:31:49,303
‎You're way more important
‎than any of that.

367
00:31:49,887 --> 00:31:52,306
‎So why the hell
‎are you doing this to yourself?

368
00:32:06,696 --> 00:32:08,781
‎Has this Pi-o Kang guy
‎just completely gone mad?

369
00:32:08,865 --> 00:32:12,160
‎If you can't handle the pressure,
‎you shouldn't be competing at all.

370
00:32:12,744 --> 00:32:15,663
‎Seriously, how can one person
‎cause this much trouble for everyone else?

371
00:32:17,081 --> 00:32:19,250
‎All right, let's head in.

372
00:32:19,333 --> 00:32:21,627
‎Anna, you should
‎get some rest for tomorrow.

373
00:32:22,462 --> 00:32:23,296
‎You're right.

374
00:32:25,548 --> 00:32:26,382
‎Wait.

375
00:32:27,842 --> 00:32:28,801
‎Is that…

376
00:32:30,053 --> 00:32:31,179
‎really true?

377
00:32:32,764 --> 00:32:36,476
‎You are not lying to me, are you?

378
00:32:37,894 --> 00:32:38,853
‎What?

379
00:32:39,896 --> 00:32:41,397
‎Are you saying one of us did it?

380
00:32:44,776 --> 00:32:45,943
‎Sorry.

381
00:32:49,906 --> 00:32:50,740
‎Look.

382
00:32:51,240 --> 00:32:54,035
‎No one went out into the garden. See?

383
00:32:54,118 --> 00:32:56,287
‎Isn't there a CCTV in the hallway?

384
00:32:56,954 --> 00:32:59,582
‎That area is for staff only,
‎so there are no cameras.

385
00:32:59,665 --> 00:33:00,583
‎Pi-o.

386
00:33:01,209 --> 00:33:04,462
‎Maybe you should try to think carefully
‎about where you might have left it.

387
00:33:05,254 --> 00:33:06,923
‎If it turns up somewhere else later,

388
00:33:07,673 --> 00:33:09,050
‎this could end badly for you.

389
00:33:10,134 --> 00:33:13,513
‎Are you sure this isn't a panic attack
‎from too much pressure?

390
00:33:13,596 --> 00:33:15,139
‎Maybe you should withdraw

391
00:33:15,223 --> 00:33:16,349
‎and go see a doctor.

392
00:33:33,157 --> 00:33:35,118
‎DAY 4 OF THE FINAL ROUND

393
00:33:35,201 --> 00:33:36,953
‎-Bye, guys.
‎-Good luck.

394
00:33:37,036 --> 00:33:38,246
‎You got this.

395
00:33:39,205 --> 00:33:40,665
‎-Thanks.
‎-You can do it.

396
00:34:01,060 --> 00:34:02,854
‎KANG PI-O

397
00:34:02,937 --> 00:34:04,188
‎-Let go of me!
‎-Out, now!

398
00:34:05,148 --> 00:34:06,607
‎What a psychopath!

399
00:34:06,691 --> 00:34:08,025
‎You know what? Try that again,

400
00:34:08,109 --> 00:34:09,569
‎and I'll smash your face.

401
00:35:09,003 --> 00:35:11,255
‎Turn it off. It's too bright.

402
00:35:11,339 --> 00:35:14,550
‎Get up and eat some of this
‎before you get sick.

403
00:35:23,351 --> 00:35:26,187
‎How long are you going to lie around?
‎What about practice?

404
00:35:28,231 --> 00:35:29,273
‎Get out.

405
00:35:33,778 --> 00:35:36,572
‎You shouldn't be lounging around.

406
00:35:37,657 --> 00:35:40,117
‎I said I'd wipe the floor with you
‎if you didn't practice hard.

407
00:35:47,625 --> 00:35:48,751
‎I'm going to withdraw.

408
00:35:57,134 --> 00:35:57,969
‎What?

409
00:35:58,552 --> 00:35:59,428
‎Hey.

410
00:36:00,346 --> 00:36:02,181
‎What kind of nonsense is that?

411
00:36:03,182 --> 00:36:05,434
‎Why would you withdraw
‎over some sheet music?

412
00:36:06,477 --> 00:36:08,437
‎Have you really lost your mind?

413
00:36:09,063 --> 00:36:09,981
‎Yeah.

414
00:36:12,608 --> 00:36:13,985
‎Maybe I have.

415
00:36:14,819 --> 00:36:16,028
‎I don't know if I hallucinated

416
00:36:17,488 --> 00:36:19,490
‎or if I was out of my mind.

417
00:36:22,660 --> 00:36:24,036
‎I don't know if I lost it

418
00:36:25,663 --> 00:36:27,164
‎or if it was stolen.

419
00:36:28,833 --> 00:36:30,251
‎Still,

420
00:36:30,334 --> 00:36:32,878
‎there's no way
‎you haven't memorized it already.

421
00:36:35,339 --> 00:36:36,841
‎Losing it doesn't mean--

422
00:36:36,924 --> 00:36:38,384
‎Memorizing it isn't the issue.

423
00:36:39,885 --> 00:36:41,429
‎I couldn't interpret it.

424
00:36:42,555 --> 00:36:45,516
‎And that scared me.

425
00:36:46,976 --> 00:36:48,227
‎Even if I compete…

426
00:36:51,772 --> 00:36:53,065
‎I'll just get eliminated.

427
00:36:55,651 --> 00:36:56,902
‎I know it.

428
00:36:58,487 --> 00:37:00,031
‎This is probably for the best.

429
00:37:01,449 --> 00:37:02,408
‎The truth is…

430
00:37:04,702 --> 00:37:05,870
‎I already knew.

431
00:37:06,996 --> 00:37:08,539
‎I knew entering this competition

432
00:37:09,582 --> 00:37:11,500
‎was too ambitious of me.

433
00:37:15,338 --> 00:37:17,798
‎And I knew becoming a great pianist

434
00:37:18,883 --> 00:37:22,261
‎was too big a dream for me.

435
00:37:24,221 --> 00:37:25,181
‎But…

436
00:37:27,016 --> 00:37:28,601
‎I loved the piano too much…

437
00:37:30,936 --> 00:37:32,480
‎to give it up.

438
00:37:34,523 --> 00:37:37,777
‎I loved music too much.

439
00:37:38,986 --> 00:37:39,904
‎That's why

440
00:37:41,197 --> 00:37:42,615
‎I did whatever I could

441
00:37:43,824 --> 00:37:45,951
‎to play those beautiful songs‎…

442
00:37:47,870 --> 00:37:49,205
‎with my own hands.

443
00:37:49,830 --> 00:37:51,749
‎I knew I was being too ambitious,

444
00:37:53,084 --> 00:37:54,251
‎but I couldn't give up.

445
00:38:01,842 --> 00:38:03,094
‎I'm walking away now…

446
00:38:05,137 --> 00:38:06,472
‎from this unrequited love.

447
00:38:10,601 --> 00:38:13,938
‎I feel like I've done all that I can.

448
00:38:17,358 --> 00:38:18,275
‎And…

449
00:38:20,027 --> 00:38:21,779
‎I owe you an apology.

450
00:38:24,323 --> 00:38:26,367
‎I projected my inferiority and self-doubt

451
00:38:27,076 --> 00:38:30,287
‎onto you for no reason.

452
00:38:30,955 --> 00:38:32,540
‎I'm going to quit now…

453
00:38:35,042 --> 00:38:37,044
‎but I hope you'll keep going.

454
00:38:41,257 --> 00:38:42,299
‎Please leave.

455
00:38:43,551 --> 00:38:44,552
‎I want to sleep.

456
00:39:18,669 --> 00:39:20,463
‎This is all your fault.

457
00:39:20,546 --> 00:39:21,881
‎It's all your fault!

458
00:39:24,300 --> 00:39:25,759
‎I owe you an apology.

459
00:39:27,428 --> 00:39:29,388
‎I projected my inferiority and self-doubt

460
00:39:30,639 --> 00:39:32,308
‎onto you for no reason.

461
00:39:36,937 --> 00:39:39,231
‎But I need you to promise me something.

462
00:39:39,815 --> 00:39:41,775
‎If you're just going to
‎play a supporting role,

463
00:39:43,152 --> 00:39:44,236
‎stop right now.

464
00:41:36,682 --> 00:41:39,101
‎CHOI JEONG-YO

465
00:42:23,646 --> 00:42:24,730
‎I've memorized everything.

466
00:42:25,564 --> 00:42:26,815
‎Take it if you need it.

467
00:42:38,952 --> 00:42:40,245
‎IN SYNC WITH THE WIND INSTRUMENTS

468
00:42:40,329 --> 00:42:41,330
‎LISTEN TO THE RHYTHM

469
00:42:43,791 --> 00:42:45,668
‎ADD ANOTHER TIMBRE,
‎LIKE I'M HOLDING MY BREATH

470
00:42:45,751 --> 00:42:47,086
‎EASY ON THE CRESCENDO

471
00:43:37,761 --> 00:43:41,682
‎LAST DAY OF THE FINAL ROUND

472
00:44:18,260 --> 00:44:19,261
‎Good luck.

473
00:44:20,929 --> 00:44:21,805
‎Thank you.

474
00:44:48,791 --> 00:44:53,462
‎We are at the Prague Harmonie
‎International Competition finals venue.

475
00:44:53,545 --> 00:44:56,965
‎Today is the final round,
‎featuring the two finalists.

476
00:44:57,049 --> 00:45:00,969
‎Following their exceptional
‎semifinal performances,

477
00:45:01,053 --> 00:45:04,181
‎all attention is focused
‎on today's event.

478
00:45:10,145 --> 00:45:12,189
‎The assigned piece is a nightmare,

479
00:45:12,272 --> 00:45:14,149
‎so there's no telling
‎how this will play out.

480
00:45:14,733 --> 00:45:16,818
‎Don't worry. Jeong-yo will do great.

481
00:45:41,802 --> 00:45:42,678
‎See you again.

482
00:45:43,428 --> 00:45:44,263
‎Thank you.

483
00:45:49,017 --> 00:45:51,937
‎You are the final performer
‎of the competition.

484
00:45:52,020 --> 00:45:55,357
‎We are all looking forward
‎to a wonderful performance.

485
00:45:56,483 --> 00:45:57,526
‎Okay. Thank you.

486
00:45:59,152 --> 00:46:00,821
‎-Bye.
‎-Bye.

487
00:46:03,657 --> 00:46:04,616
‎Thank you.

488
00:46:49,494 --> 00:46:51,163
‎What just happened?

489
00:46:51,955 --> 00:46:53,790
‎Is that really the Kang Pi-o I know?

490
00:47:26,406 --> 00:47:29,743
‎Mr. Kang. That was amazing, really.

491
00:47:29,826 --> 00:47:30,827
‎Thank you.

492
00:47:31,745 --> 00:47:33,997
‎Your performance is so unique.

493
00:47:34,081 --> 00:47:37,000
‎If you do just as well in the free piece,
‎you're bound to win.

494
00:47:52,557 --> 00:47:54,601
‎Did you check if the money came in?

495
00:47:54,685 --> 00:47:55,686
‎I did.

496
00:47:57,020 --> 00:47:58,897
‎Then where's my advance payment?

497
00:47:58,980 --> 00:48:00,649
‎Do I look like a pushover to you?

498
00:48:00,732 --> 00:48:02,984
‎I said you'd get paid after the job.

499
00:48:03,068 --> 00:48:04,486
‎What's with all the whining?

500
00:49:30,197 --> 00:49:31,865
‎Where are we going now?

501
00:49:33,325 --> 00:49:37,621
‎Isn't this the opposite direction
‎from the concert hall?

502
00:49:39,122 --> 00:49:40,290
‎Excuse me.

503
00:49:40,373 --> 00:49:41,625
‎Stop, stop!

504
00:49:41,708 --> 00:49:43,502
‎I want to go to the toilet!

505
00:49:44,961 --> 00:49:46,004
‎Are you listening to me?

506
00:49:46,087 --> 00:49:48,131
‎I said I need to go to the restroom!

507
00:49:49,466 --> 00:49:50,300
‎Cut the crap!

508
00:49:50,884 --> 00:49:53,053
‎Or else I'll put a bullet
‎through your head.

509
00:50:27,754 --> 00:50:30,715
‎Watch it before you drive us into a grave.

510
00:50:30,799 --> 00:50:31,716
‎No, you watch it.

511
00:50:31,800 --> 00:50:33,593
‎Don't get blood splatter in the car.

512
00:50:34,886 --> 00:50:38,765
‎Who do you think you are?
‎Don't tell me what to do.

513
00:50:38,849 --> 00:50:40,308
‎You want me to kill you first?

514
00:50:40,392 --> 00:50:42,686
‎Just focus on driving, you piece of crap!

515
00:53:02,158 --> 00:53:03,827
‎Bravo!

516
00:53:54,711 --> 00:53:55,879
‎Where did he disappear to?

517
00:53:55,962 --> 00:53:58,381
‎I don't know.
‎We can't get in touch with security.

518
00:54:02,052 --> 00:54:03,011
‎Excuse me.

519
00:54:03,094 --> 00:54:04,512
‎Is something going on?

520
00:54:05,013 --> 00:54:06,014
‎We're not sure yet,

521
00:54:06,097 --> 00:54:08,058
‎but the last finalist
‎still hasn't arrived.

522
00:54:13,938 --> 00:54:18,193
‎We regret to inform you
‎of some unfortunate news.

523
00:54:18,902 --> 00:54:21,196
‎The final contestant of the competition,

524
00:54:21,279 --> 00:54:24,741
‎Jeong-yo Choi, has gone missing.

525
00:54:25,617 --> 00:54:29,788
‎Therefore, today's final performance
‎has been canceled.

526
00:54:30,663 --> 00:54:33,458
‎The decision regarding the award ceremony

527
00:54:33,541 --> 00:54:37,921
‎will be decided as soon as the situation
‎has been assessed.

528
00:54:38,838 --> 00:54:39,672
‎Thank you.

529
00:54:46,763 --> 00:54:48,264
‎What do you mean Jeong-yo is missing?

530
00:54:48,348 --> 00:54:50,475
‎We don't know anything yet.

531
00:54:50,558 --> 00:54:52,936
‎We reported the situation to the police.

532
00:54:53,019 --> 00:54:55,271
‎But for the time being,

533
00:54:55,355 --> 00:54:57,190
‎please return to your accommodations

534
00:54:57,273 --> 00:55:00,068
‎and then we'll contact you individually.

535
00:55:23,800 --> 00:55:25,969
‎-Where have you been?
‎-You scared me!

536
00:55:45,989 --> 00:55:48,575
‎Why won't you even tell us
‎what you've found so far?

537
00:55:49,242 --> 00:55:50,451
‎Was he kidnapped?

538
00:55:50,535 --> 00:55:51,786
‎Was it an accident?

539
00:55:51,870 --> 00:55:54,289
‎Have you identified the driver
‎and the guard yet?

540
00:55:54,372 --> 00:55:55,206
‎Okay.

541
00:55:55,290 --> 00:55:57,375
‎There's nothing we can share at this time.

542
00:55:57,458 --> 00:56:01,171
‎What do you mean you can't tell me?
‎I'm his guardian!

543
00:56:01,254 --> 00:56:02,088
‎Stop, Hyun-jeong.

544
00:56:02,172 --> 00:56:04,299
‎These people don't know anything yet.

545
00:56:04,382 --> 00:56:07,093
‎How could something like this happen?

546
00:56:07,760 --> 00:56:08,928
‎What's going on?

547
00:56:09,512 --> 00:56:11,431
‎Is it true Jeong-yo has gone missing?

548
00:56:12,307 --> 00:56:13,725
‎Police are currently investigating

549
00:56:13,808 --> 00:56:16,352
‎whether this disappearance is related
‎to the recent kidnapping attacks

550
00:56:16,436 --> 00:56:17,437
‎carried out by…

551
00:56:27,155 --> 00:56:28,281
‎Where's Jeong-yo?

552
00:56:28,907 --> 00:56:30,116
‎They haven't found him yet.

553
00:56:32,076 --> 00:56:34,871
‎They haven't even located the car
‎he was in.

554
00:56:34,954 --> 00:56:36,039
‎We'll have to wait longer

555
00:56:37,415 --> 00:56:38,958
‎for the police investigation.

556
00:56:44,881 --> 00:56:46,633
‎Pi-o, are you okay?

557
00:56:50,803 --> 00:56:52,263
‎Don't worry too much.

558
00:56:54,390 --> 00:56:55,642
‎He'll be okay.

559
00:56:56,309 --> 00:56:58,102
‎They'll find him soon.

560
00:56:59,646 --> 00:57:01,105
‎I'm sure there was just a mix-up.

561
00:57:02,565 --> 00:57:06,236
‎So don't worry too much.

562
00:57:08,905 --> 00:57:09,739
‎Mom.

563
00:57:10,949 --> 00:57:11,866
‎Mom.

564
00:57:13,076 --> 00:57:14,244
‎Mom, did you…

565
00:57:48,820 --> 00:57:53,616
‎The winner of the Prague Harmonie
‎International Competition is

566
00:57:53,700 --> 00:57:56,035
‎Mr. Pi-o Kang.

567
00:58:50,840 --> 00:58:55,553
‎2026

568
00:58:59,474 --> 00:59:01,684
‎You look tired from the long trip.

569
00:59:01,768 --> 00:59:02,852
‎I'm fine.

570
00:59:02,935 --> 00:59:04,771
‎Did you secure the practice room?

571
00:59:05,521 --> 00:59:07,023
‎It was too late to find one,

572
00:59:07,106 --> 00:59:09,984
‎so we arranged a bar
‎across from the hotel.

573
00:59:10,068 --> 00:59:12,153
‎So you can use it after it closes.

574
00:59:12,987 --> 00:59:14,197
‎Will that be all right?

575
00:59:14,781 --> 00:59:16,074
‎That should be okay for now.

576
01:00:42,660 --> 01:00:44,579
‎I'VE MEMORIZED EVERYTHING.
‎TAKE IT IF YOU NEED IT!

577
01:01:04,682 --> 01:01:06,809
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

578
01:01:06,893 --> 01:01:09,145
‎About that Choi Jeong-yo rumor…

579
01:01:09,228 --> 01:01:11,063
‎People say you were behind it.

580
01:01:11,147 --> 01:01:13,191
‎It's because of you.

581
01:01:13,274 --> 01:01:16,694
‎I found someone in Romania
‎who said they saw Mr. Choi.

582
01:01:16,778 --> 01:01:17,904
‎It was this man.

583
01:01:17,987 --> 01:01:19,614
‎I'd like to ask him myself.

584
01:01:19,697 --> 01:01:21,949
‎What did you do to Jeong-yo?

585
01:01:22,450 --> 01:01:23,618
‎What's in it for me?

586
01:01:24,702 --> 01:01:25,536
‎Tell me now!

587
01:01:26,120 --> 01:01:27,288
‎Do you even know how special he was?

588
01:01:27,789 --> 01:01:29,415
‎What exactly are you trying to confirm?

589
01:01:30,208 --> 01:01:31,793
‎Proof that Mr. Choi is alive?

590
01:01:32,460 --> 01:01:33,711
‎Or proof of his death?

591
01:01:35,338 --> 01:01:40,343
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim

